    "name_suffix": "_2026",
    "teacher_markdown": "### Example issues students might identify\r\n- **Perceivable:** low color contrast, missing alt text, text that is difficult to read\r\n- **Operable:** buttons that are too small, hard-to-use navigation, interactions that are difficult to complete\r\n- **Understandable:** unclear labels, confusing instructions, inconsistent layout\r\n- **Robust:** missing semantic headings, poor structure for screen readers, elements that may not work well across devices\r\n\r\n\r\n### What to look for\r\nStudents do not need to fix every issue they identify. The goal is for them to:\r\n1. identify real accessibility concerns in their own work,\r\n2. connect those concerns to the POUR framework, and\r\n3. apply at least 1-2 meaningful improvements.\r\n",
